Entain agrees AU$185 million settlement to end Austrac AML case in Australia

Entain's Australian subsidiary has reached a preliminary agreement with financial crime regulator Austrac to settle civil penalty proceedings over anti-money laundering and counter-terrorism financing failings, iGaming Business reports. Entain Australia would pay a AU$185 million ($122.7 million) penalty plus Austrac's costs, above the AU$100 million provision it had set aside. The deal still needs approval from Austrac, Entain's board and the Federal Court, which had been due to start a trial next week. Barclays and Goodbody analysts called it a positive step that removes a long-running overhang on the shares.

